{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"b08375311d7a522f","name":"card_unit_french_75","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/France/units/card_unit_french_75","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"FRENCH 75","text":"The first unit you deploy each turn gets +1+1.","flavorText":"The French 75 mm field gun was a quick-firing field artillery, produced from 1897 to 1940. Officially the gun was called Matériel de 75mm Mle 1897, but commonly known as the French 75, simply the 75 and Soixante-Quinze (French for \"seventy-five\"). The gun was designed as an anti-personnel weapon, delivering large volumes of time-fused shrapnel shells on enemy targets. Large numbers of 75’s were still in use in 1939, 4,500 of them in France alone. Many of the guns were captured by the Germans who used a modified anti-tank version named 7.5 cm Pak 97/38, which was mainly used in 1942 against the Soviet T-34 and KV tanks.","faction":"France","type":"artillery","rarity":"Common","cost":4,"operationCost":1,"attack":2,"defense":4},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_french_75","title":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_unit_french_75_title","SourceString":"FRENCH 75","LocalizedString":"FRENCH 75"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::artillery","attack":2,"defense":4,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::France","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_unit_french_75_text","SourceString":"The first unit you deploy each turn gets +1+1.","LocalizedString":"The first unit you deploy each turn gets +1+1."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_unit_french_75_history","SourceString":"The French 75 mm field gun was a quick-firing field artillery, produced from 1897 to 1940. Officially the gun was called Matériel de 75mm Mle 1897, but commonly known as the French 75, simply the 75 and Soixante-Quinze (French for \"seventy-five\"). The gun was designed as an anti-personnel weapon, delivering large volumes of time-fused shrapnel shells on enemy targets. Large numbers of 75’s were still in use in 1939, 4,500 of them in France alone. Many of the guns were captured by the Germans who used a modified anti-tank version named 7.5 cm Pak 97/38, which was mainly used in 1942 against the Soviet T-34 and KV tanks.","LocalizedString":"The French 75 mm field gun was a quick-firing field artillery, produced from 1897 to 1940. Officially the gun was called Matériel de 75mm Mle 1897, but commonly known as the French 75, simply the 75 and Soixante-Quinze (French for \"seventy-five\"). The gun was designed as an anti-personnel weapon, delivering large volumes of time-fused shrapnel shells on enemy targets. Large numbers of 75’s were still in use in 1939, 4,500 of them in France alone. Many of the guns were captured by the Germans who used a modified anti-tank version named 7.5 cm Pak 97/38, which was mainly used in 1942 against the Soviet T-34 and KV tanks."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Expansion2019","isInPermanentPool":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Passive","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnEndOfTurn","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardPlayedFromHand"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Infantry_Move_FX'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Units/Infantry_Move_FX.0"},"soundMoveToFrontline":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Infantry_Move_FX'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Units/Infantry_Move_FX.0"},"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Explosion_Small'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/Explosion_Small.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/France/t_arty_french.t_arty_french","SubPathString":""},"artist":"French WWII Poster","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/FRENCH_75.FRENCH_75","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":378.0},"historyPhotoSource":"https://ww2db.com/","historyPhotoAuthor":" ","historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_unit_french_75_photo","